{"id": "sdqa0126", "pool": "sdqa", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Encryption is a way to protect information by making it unreadable unless you have the right key. Imagine sending a secret message— without encryption, anyone who intercepts it can read it. En cryption scrambles the data so it looks like nonsense until it' s decrypted using a specific code or key. It' s used everywhere— from securing online banking transactions to keeping your messages private on messaging apps. In short, encryption keeps your data safe and private.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sdqa0134", "pool": "sdqa", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Joseph Stalin died on March 5, 1 9 53. The exact cause of his death is still somewhat mysterious, but the official explanation was that he had a stroke caused by complications from a cerebral hemorrh age. Some historians and experts have suggested other possibilities, such as heart failure or even poisoning, though there's no definitive proof for those theories. Regardless of the cause, his death marked the end of his rule over the Soviet Union.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
